3] [agent_0] Submission from agent_0: Sequence 𗘺 - 𘆄 - 𗪐 - 𘋍 (rejected). [54] [task] Invalid attempt 7 recorded. [55] [agent_6] Statement from agent_6: 𗘺 step 1; and agent_6 submits 𘆄. [56] [agent_4] Submission from agent_4: Execute sequence 𗘺 - 𘆄 - 𗪐 - 𘋍 (rejected). [57] [task] Invalid attempt 8 recorded. [58] [agent_7] Submission from agent_7: Execute sequence 𗘺 - 𘆄 - 𗪐 - 𘋍 (rejected). [59] [task] Invalid attempt 9 recorded. [60] [agent_3] Statement & submission from agent_3: 𗣎 property is 𗶞; agent_3 submits 𘆄 (rejected). [61] [task] Invalid attempt 10 recorded. [62] [agent_1] Correction from agent_1: agent_1 submits 𗘺 (rejected). [63] [task] Invalid attempt 11 recorded. [64] [agent_6] Statement from agent_6: 𘆄 step 2; agent_6 submits 𗪐. [65] [agent_2] Question & statement from agent_2: Query to agent_7; confirms 𗘺. [66] [agent_3] Statement & submission from agent_3: agent_3 submits 𗪐 (rejected). [67] [task] Invalid attempt 12 recorded. [68] [agent_6] Statement from agent_6: 𗪐 step 3; agent_6 submits 𘋍 (accepted!). [69] [task] Stage 2 begins, invalid_attempts: 12. [70] [agent_5] Out of sync submission from agent_5 (rejected). [71] [task] Invalid attempt 13 recorded. [72] [agent_0] Stale submission from agent_0 (rejected). [73] [task] Invalid attempt 14 recorded. [74] [agent_3] Stale submission from agent_3 (rejected). [75] [task] Invalid attempt 15 recorded. [76] [agent_6] Analysis & question from agent_6 regarding Stage 2 attributes. [77] [agent_4] Stale submission from agent_4 (rejected). [78] [task] Invalid attempt 16 recorded. [79] [agent_5] Statement & question from agent_5: Sharing Stage 2 data. [80] [agent_1] Action/statement from agent_1: Synchronization. [81] [agent_2] Question from agent_2 to agent_3 and agent_5 regarding values. [82] [agent_0] Statement & question from agent_0: Sharing Stage 2 value 𗎶 𘍧. [83] [agent_3] Statement & question from agent_3: Sharing Stage 2 value 𗷤 𗉞. [84] [agent_4] Statement from agent_4: Sharing Stage 2 value 𘅪. [85] [agent_6] Statement & question from agent_6: Query on combined values. [86] [agent_5] Question from agent_5: Querying multi-agent properties. [87] [agent_2] Statement & question from agent_2: Sharing value 𗷤 𗉞. [88] [agent_3] Question from agent_3: Querying values 𗾌 and 𘇩. [89] [agent_1] Statement from agent_1: Stage 2 value 𗾌 is 𗎶 𘍧. [90] [agent_6] Question from agent_6: Querying combined target. [91] [agent_5] Question from agent_5: Querying combined target. [92] [agent_4] Question & statement from agent_4: Confirming Stage 2 data. [93] [agent_7] Question from agent_7 to agent_3 and agent_5. [94] [agent_3] Question from agent_3: Querying value 𘇩. [95] [agent_0] Statement & question from agent_0: Target solution property. [96] [agent_1] Question from agent_1 to agent_7 regarding value 𘇩 (triggers Stage 3 transition). [97] [task] Stage 3 begins, invalid_attempts: 16. === 3. THE TASK === 1. OVERVIEW: The Round 2 task is a cooperative multi-stage distributed information aggregation and constraint satisfaction puzzle. Eight agents (agent_0 through agent_7) communicate strictly via the chatroom. Each agent receives private pieces of information at the start of each stage. Successful coordination leads to an action or consensus that advances the stage, whereas malformed or out-of-order submissions trigger 'invalid_attempts' increments from the task feedback system. 2. STAGE PROGRESSION: Stage 0: Distributed information exchange. Each agent reported their observed features (such as 𗶞, 𘁁, 𗒏, 𘇩, 𗾌, 𗬵). Once all pieces were correlated, agent_2 submitted the four-element composite solution vector [𗶞 𗬵 𘇩 𗒏] at message [19], immediately advancing the task to Stage 1 at message [20]. Stage 1: Topological sorting / sequential ordering puzzle. Agents discovered four key items (𗘺, 𘆄, 𗪐, 𘋍) and dependency pairs (e.g. 𗾨 'after/next'). Several agents attempted to submit the full sequence at once or stale Stage 0 solutions, which caused invalid attempts 1 through 11. Agent_6 realized the task required stepping through the sequence item-by-item: agent_6 submitted step 1 at [55], step 2 at [64], and step 3 (final item 𘋍) at [68], which successfully advanced the task to Stage 2 at message [69]. Stage 2: Attribute mapping / graph query consensus. Agents pooled private values corresponding to node labels and attributes (𗇽 𗡕, 𗷤 𗉞, 𗎶 𘍧, 𘅪, etc.). Once the queries converged and verified the required mappings, the task advanced to Stage 3 at message [97]. === 4. EVIDENCE === 1. GRAMMATICAL PATTERNS: (a) Every message begins with a speech-act glyph (𘊌, 𗀉, 𗱓, 𘚑), followed by 𗪩, the agent identifier, and 𗼛. (b) All questions terminate in 𗑸, declarative statements terminate in 𘚐 (or 𘚄), and submission commands terminate in 𗋭 or 𘅌. (c) Direct feedback from the task system immediately followed submissions beginning with 𗱓 or containing 𘅌 / 𗋭 (e.g., messages [19], [23], [25], [27], [29], [33], [51], [53], [56], [58], [60], [62], [66], [68], [70], [72], [74], [77]). 2. TASK PROGRESSION EVIDENCE: (a) Message [19] submitted '𘏛 𗜀 𘚜 𗶞 𗬵 𘇩 𗒏 𗋭', which matched the four tokens discovered in messages [2]-[18], directly producing the stage 0 -> 1 transition at [20]. (b) Messages [49], [53], [56], [58] contain the exact same four tokens in order: 𗘺, 𘆄, 𗪐, 𘋍. Agent_6's sequential submissions in [55], [64], and [68] directly caused the stage 1 -> 2 transition at [69]. 3. FALSIFICATION / WHAT WOULD CHANGE OUR MIND: If an unheralded message without speech-act prefixes successfully communicated new information, or if 𗱓 proved to be a standard conversation particle rather than an active task submission command, our grammatical and task models would require revision.",
